## leaf wait --help
Usage: leaf wait [OPTIONS] PAGE

  Watch every page this session holds \u2014 plus PAGE, claimed first, when given.

  Print one page's complete ordered batch, conversation context, and response
  requirements as an immutable delivery. `leaf delivery read <id>` reads that
  same delivery.

  If output is truncated, acknowledge nothing; rerun with enough output capacity
  for the whole batch. If you handle the batch yourself, read it fully, then
  acknowledge it before any other work. If forwarding it, or if its guidance
  holds the acknowledgement until a request reaches its executor, acknowledge
  once it durably arrives there. Run `leaf wait --ack <delivery-id>` in the
  background to acknowledge its captured batches and wait for the next batch
  while the page remains live.

Options:
  --ack DELIVERY_ID  Confirm receipt of this complete delivery before waiting.
  --help             Show this message and exit.

## leaf delivery claim --help
Usage: leaf delivery claim [OPTIONS] DELIVERY_ID

  Claim one still-outstanding user move from DELIVERY_ID.

  The page and subject come from the immutable delivery. Current page state is
  checked in the same transaction that writes the Working receipt, so a stale
  delivery is a successful no-op rather than a claim on newer input.

Options:
  --event EVENT_ID  Claim this delivered event instead of the first outstanding
                    user move.
  --detail TEXT     What the page says the agent is doing (default: "Reading
                    your feedback").
  --help            Show this message and exit.

## leaf delivery read --help
Usage: leaf delivery read [OPTIONS] DELIVERY_ID

  Print DELIVERY_ID with its complete batches and response requirements.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

## leaf page state --help
Usage: leaf page state [OPTIONS] PAGE

  Fold the log onto the active revision and print the result as one JSON object:
  effective content with source and edit addresses, standing state, reports,
  open Asks, conversation summaries, versions, presence, and bound data. Content
  follows the same document projection as the browser.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

## leaf conversation read --help
Usage: leaf conversation read [OPTIONS] PAGE CONVERSATION_ID

  Print one current conversation and a page of its exact event history.

Options:
  --after SEQ            [default: 0; x>=0]
  --limit INTEGER RANGE  [default: 50; 1<=x<=100]
  --help                 Show this message and exit.

## leaf conversation summarize --help
Usage: leaf conversation summarize [OPTIONS] PAGE CONVERSATION_ID

  Replace FROM through THROUGH in the panel with a Markdown summary.

  The original messages remain in the append-only transcript and can always be
  revealed. A later overlapping summary replaces this one.

Options:
  --from ID     [required]
  --through ID  [required]
  --text TEXT   summary Markdown (default: stdin)
  --json        print the summary event
  --help        Show this message and exit.

## leaf conversation title --help
Usage: leaf conversation title [OPTIONS] PAGE CONVERSATION_ID

  Name the conversation for the thread panel; repeat to rename it.

  Choose a few descriptive words when first handling a conversation. Keep the
  title stable unless its subject changes. This adds no message or reply.

Options:
  --text TEXT  short descriptive title (at most 80 characters)  [required]
  --json       print the title event
  --help       Show this message and exit.

## leaf status --help
Usage: leaf status [OPTIONS] PAGE {working|waiting|idle} [DETAIL]

  Set the agent's banner state.

  Use working with DETAIL naming your current work, or waiting with the answer
  you want from the user. Waiting without DETAIL invites text comments. Use idle
  when finished; unacknowledged input and unanswered user moves prevent it.

  With working, --on names an open conversation or page widget and requires
  DETAIL. The user sees it beside that subject as well as in the banner. Your
  next reply ends a thread claim; a version stamp with --completes ends a widget
  claim. Renew the status as work changes: a claim left after your turn ends, or
  without updates, eventually reads as stalled.

Options:
  --on SUBJECT  The open conversation or local page widget this work is about.
  --help        Show this message and exit.

## leaf comment --help
Usage: leaf comment [OPTIONS] PAGE

  Open a thread as the agent (--text or stdin): anchored where --quote or
  --section points at a passage, general where neither does \u2014 a question about
  the work as a whole.

  The user answers it in the browser. Refuses a quote the active revision does
  not hold, or holds more than once.

Options:
  --quote TEXT   passage text from the active revision
  --section ID   element ID to anchor or scope --quote
  --part ID      declared visual part within --section
  --text TEXT    comment text (default: stdin)
  --markup TEXT  widget markup to render after the text, validated here
  --json         print the comment event instead
  --help         Show this message and exit.

## leaf reply --help
Usage: leaf reply [OPTIONS] PAGE

  Post a threaded reply as the agent (--text or stdin).

  Answer user input with --for EVENT_ID. With exactly one outstanding reply in
  this turn's opened delivery, omit it to select that reply. To add a new agent
  message when no reply is owed, use --to ID --initiates.

  --quote, --section, and --part move the thread's current anchor; --detach
  removes it when the subject leaves the page. The original anchor stays in the
  log. A reply validates and activates any changed source before posting.

Options:
  --to ID         conversation message ID for --initiates; inferred when
                  answering --for
  --for EVENT_ID  delivery event whose current reply obligation this answers
  --initiates     start an agent turn only when this conversation owes no reply
  --quote TEXT    new passage text to move this thread onto
  --section ID    new element ID, or scope for --quote
  --part ID       new declared visual part within --section
  --detach        remove the current page target when its subject leaves the
                  page
  --text TEXT     reply text (default: stdin)
  --markup TEXT   widget markup to render after the text, validated here
  --awaits        the reply's prose asks the user a question
  --json          print the reply event instead
  --help          Show this message and exit.

## leaf resolve --help
Usage: leaf resolve [OPTIONS] PAGE

  Close a thread as the agent.

  The user ordinarily closes a thread; the Leaf skill's references/conversation-
  threads.md says when the agent does. Refuses a thread that asked for a version
  until a stamped version answers it. The panel names who resolved it.

Options:
  --to ID  a message in the thread to close  [required]
  --json   print the resolve event instead
  --help   Show this message and exit.

## leaf receipt --help
Usage: leaf receipt [OPTIONS] PAGE REQUEST succeeded|failed

  Record exactly one terminal host outcome for REQUEST.

Options:
  --text TEXT  host outcome (default: stdin)
  --json       print the receipt event instead
  --help       Show this message and exit.

## leaf version check --help
Usage: leaf version check [OPTIONS] PAGE

  Check PAGE/index.html.

  Runs deterministic markup checks. --render also checks the drawn page in the
  host's browser: whichever executable LEAF_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE, CHROME_PATH, or
  CHROME_BIN names, else the installed Chrome, else the first browser on PATH.

Options:
  --render  also check the rendered page in the host's browser
  --help    Show this message and exit.

## leaf version stamp --help
Usage: leaf version stamp [OPTIONS] PAGE

  Stamp PAGE/index.html with a changelog.

  Checks the exact source first, then records it as the next public version.
  Repeat --completes for each active widget work claim this version completes. A
  widget claim otherwise survives unrelated versions, and a version cannot
  silently remove its page target.

Options:
  --text TEXT         changelog text (default: stdin)
  --completes WIDGET  active widget work this version completes (repeatable)
  --json              print the note event instead
  --help              Show this message and exit.
